menu "M5 Usage Panel"

menu "Display"

config M5_USAGE_PANEL_DISPLAY_BRIGHTNESS_PERCENT
    int "Display brightness (percent)"
    range 1 100
    default 55
    help
        Panel brightness applied once at startup through M5GFX. The panel
        stays at this level; there is no screensaver dimming on this target.

choice M5_USAGE_PANEL_ROTATION
    prompt "Fixed screen orientation"
    default M5_USAGE_PANEL_ROTATION_0
    help
        The panel UI is laid out for upright portrait use, so only upright
        and inverted orientations are offered. Inverted mounting suits a
        desk stand that faces the panel away from the user.

config M5_USAGE_PANEL_ROTATION_0
    bool "0 degrees"

config M5_USAGE_PANEL_ROTATION_180
    bool "180 degrees (inverted)"

endchoice

endmenu

menu "Bluetooth"

config M5_USAGE_PANEL_BLE_ADVERTISING_PREFIX
    string "BLE advertising name prefix"
    default "QF-M5-"
    help
        Prefix of the BLE advertising name. The full name is this prefix plus
        the last two Bluetooth MAC bytes as four uppercase hex digits, for
        example QF-M5-A37F, so multiple panels stay distinguishable
        without manual coordination. Keep the prefix within 15 characters so
        prefix plus suffix fits the advertising name buffer.

        The prefix must start with QF- and contain at most 15 printable ASCII
        characters without spaces. Discovery requires both this public
        namespace and NUS; no official target registry entry is needed.
        The four-digit suffix may collide and is not a unique identity.
        Owned devices reconnect by Bluetooth address; status supplies their
        display names, capabilities and optional OTA project/target metadata.

endmenu

endmenu
